(1. Breakdown of Classical Radiation Physics) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(Towards the end of the nineteenth century, classical electromagnetic theory and) Tj T*
(equipartition of energy predicted an ultraviolet catastrophe for blackbody radiation.) Tj T*
(Rayleigh and Jeans treated cavity radiation as continuous standing waves, yielding an) Tj T*
(energy density proportional to frequency squared, which diverged as frequency grew.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(2. Planck's Energy Quantization Hypothesis) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(In 1900, Max Planck proposed that microscopic atomic oscillators in cavity walls exchange) Tj T*
(energy exclusively in discrete packets \(quanta\): E = n * h * nu, where n is an integer.) Tj T*
(This harmonic energy quantization smoothly suppressed high-frequency divergences and) Tj T*
(reproduced experimental blackbody spectra across all wavelengths.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(3. Photoelectric Effect & Einstein's Photon) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(In 1905, Albert Einstein extended Planck's concept, proposing that light propagates and) Tj T*
(interacts as discrete energy packets: E = h * nu. The maximum kinetic energy of emitted) Tj T*
(photoelectrons satisfies: K_max = h * nu - Phi, where Phi is the material work function.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(4. Wave-Particle Duality & De Broglie Hypothesis) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(Louis de Broglie postulated that if radiant energy displays particle-like properties,) Tj T*
(material particles must symmetrically exhibit wave properties with wavelength: lambda = h / p.) Tj T*
(This established the foundation for wave mechanics and the Schrodinger equation.) Tj T*
